---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import Card from '@components/Card.astro';
import profileImage from '@assets/images/profile.webp';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Meet Andrew Noblet - A curious software engineer with global perspective. Born in Chile, lived across Puerto Rico, Ohio, and New York. Passionate about minimalist philosophy and accessible web development."
>
  <div class="max-width-56 width-100 margin-auto column flex gap-2">
    <span></span>
    <section class="gap grid justify-content-center text-align-center">
      <img
        src={profileImage.src}
        alt="Andrew Noblet profile photo"
        class="margin-auto border-radius-50 box-shadow-tertiary block height-16 width-16 object-fit-cover relative z-index-1"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        width={profileImage.width}
        height={profileImage.height}
      />
      <h1>Meet Andrew Noblet</h1>
      <p>
        Hello! I'm <strong>Andrew Noblet</strong>, a curious soul with a truly
        global perspective—born in Chile and shaped by rich experiences living
        in Puerto Rico's vibrant culture, Ohio's midwestern values, and now New
        York's endless energy. Each place taught me something different:
        resilience from my Chilean roots, warmth and community from Puerto Rico,
        steady determination from Ohio, and boundless possibility from New York.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm passionate about exploring life through diverse interests that span
        the physical, creative, and intellectual. Whether I'm building with my
        favorite technologies like Astro and Lit, tinkering with smart home
        automation, or diving deep into Eastern philosophy and Greek mythology,
        I believe in living authentically and embracing the adventure that each
        day brings.
      </p>
    </section>
    <Card>
      <h2>Personal Facts</h2>
      <ul class="column flex gap-0-5 padding-horizontal-1">
        <li><strong>Full Name:</strong> Andrew Noblet</li>
        <li><strong>Born in:</strong> Chile</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Life Journey:</strong> Chile → Puerto Rico → Ohio → <strong
            >New York</strong
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub:</strong>
          <a href="https://github.com/anoblet" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >anoblet</a
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Philosophy:</strong> Eastern wisdom meets Western curiosity—drawing
          from Confucianism, Buddhism, and Shintoism while staying grounded in practical
          application
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Favorite Tech:</strong> Astro, Lit, Linux, and the pnpm workflow—tools
          that embrace simplicity and performance
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Motto:</strong> "Less noise, more meaning"
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fun Fact:</strong> I love a good plate of spaghetti, but you won't
          catch me eating lamb!
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Card>
    <Card>
      <h2>Hobbies & Passions</h2>
      <div class="column flex gap">
        <div>
          <h3>Physical & Outdoor</h3>
          <p>
            Skateboarding has been a passion since childhood—passionate enough
            that at 14, I successfully petitioned my town to build a skatepark!
            The persistence paid off, and seeing that project come to life
            taught me the power of advocacy and community engagement. I also
            love snowboarding for the pure exhilaration and bike riding through
            New York's diverse neighborhoods, connecting with the rhythm and
            flow of movement.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Creative & Technical</h3>
          <p>
            Playing guitar gives me a creative outlet that balances my technical
            work. My 3D printing projects range from practical household
            solutions to experimental designs—there's something satisfying about
            bringing digital ideas into physical reality. Smart home technology
            fascinates me; I love building automated systems that make daily
            life more efficient while staying true to minimalist principles.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Intellectual Pursuits</h3>
          <p>
            I'm deeply interested in politics and how policy shapes our digital
            future, and I find history essential for understanding today's
            technological and social patterns. Eastern philosophy—Confucianism's
            harmony, Buddhist mindfulness, and Shinto reverence for natural
            balance—guides my approach to both code architecture and life
            decisions. Greek mythology reminds me that human struggles with
            technology, power, and purpose are as old as civilization itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Card>
    <Card>
      <h2>Life Philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        My worldview is shaped by a blend of Eastern wisdom traditions that
        complement each other beautifully. <strong>Confucian</strong> principles
        of harmony and continuous learning influence how I approach both code architecture
        and relationships—everything should be balanced, purposeful, and constantly
        improving. <strong>Buddhist</strong> mindfulness keeps me present and compassionate,
        especially valuable in our fast-paced digital world. <strong
          >Shinto</strong
        > reverence for natural balance reminds me to respect both the digital and
        physical environments I inhabit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Greek mythology grounds me in the understanding that human struggles
        with technology, power, and purpose are timeless. Whether it's
        Prometheus bringing fire to humanity or Pandora's box of unintended
        consequences, these ancient stories offer profound insights for
        navigating modern innovation responsibly.
      </p>
      <p>
        All of this culminates in my core belief: <em
          >less noise, more meaning</em
        >. Whether I'm writing code, building relationships, or making life
        decisions, I strive for simplicity, intentionality, and authentic
        connection.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card>
      <h2>Early Adventures</h2>
      <p>
        My curiosity started young and led to some memorable learning
        experiences. At <strong>13</strong>, I built my first website at <strong
          >nebulae.org</strong
        >
        and dove deep into PHP development with php-nuke—my first taste of content
        management systems. This was back when Adobe Dreamweaver was the tool of
        choice, and I used it religiously for every project.
      </p>
      <p>
        I was so fascinated by web development that I bought a
        several-hundred-page book on Adobe ColdFusion and read it
        cover-to-cover, absorbing every detail about server-side programming. By
        my teens, I was ambitious enough to build my own water-cooled computer
        system—let's just say I learned the importance of preparation and leak
        testing the hard way. Towels were definitely needed, and the experience
        taught me valuable lessons about both hardware and humility! 😅
      </p>
      <p>
        Meanwhile, my skateboarding passion was equally strong. At <strong
          >14</strong
        >, I didn't just wish for better facilities—I petitioned my town council
        to build a skatepark, presenting a case for youth engagement and
        community recreation. They listened, and the skatepark became a reality,
        teaching me that persistence and clear communication can turn ideas into
        action.
      </p>
      <p>
        These early adventures shaped my core belief that curiosity,
        persistence, preparation, and a willingness to learn from mistakes
        (sometimes messy ones!) are the best tools for any journey.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card>
      <h2>Life in New York</h2>
      <p>
        New York perfectly matches my energy for exploration and growth. The
        city's diversity mirrors my own global journey, and I love how every
        neighborhood offers something new to discover. Whether I'm exploring on
        my bike through different boroughs, testing out a new 3D printing
        technique in my apartment, or finding quiet spots to read about history
        and philosophy, the city provides endless opportunities for curiosity
        and connection.
      </p>
      <p>
        The tech community here is incredible—I particularly enjoy connecting
        with people who share my passion for open-source development, minimalist
        design principles, and building technology that genuinely improves
        people's lives. There's something special about discussing the parallels
        between ancient Stoicism and modern minimalism over coffee, or sharing
        skateboarding stories that bridge generations and cultures.
      </p>
      <p>
        Living here reinforces my belief that the best solutions—whether in
        code, design, or life—often come from embracing complexity while
        maintaining simplicity at the core. It's the perfect environment for
        someone who appreciates both cutting-edge innovation and timeless
        wisdom.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <section class="gap grid justify-content-center text-align-center">
      <h2>Let's Connect!</h2>
      <p>
        Let's connect and discuss how my experience can help bring your vision
        to life.
      </p>
      <div class="gap grid">
        <button-component href="/contact"> Get in Touch </button-component>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import '@components/button';
</script>
